VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-passive-voice",{"titre":"Active and passive voices","duree":35,"famille":"Citizenship and human rights","agir":"Change sentences from the active to the passive voice and choose the voice that fits the message","accroche":"“Workers in Douala make chocolate.” “Chocolate is made in Douala.” Same fact, two voices. Why would a journalist choose the second?","intro":"Mbah writes an article for the school magazine about a cocoa factory in Douala. His sentences will help you master the passive voice.","objectifs":["recognise the active and the passive voice","form the passive (be + past participle) in the main tenses","use by + agent only when necessary","choose the voice according to what is important in the message"],"enquete":{"titre":"The school magazine article","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A factory hall with a conveyor belt carrying bags of cocoa beans that come out as chocolate bars; a student journalist takes notes' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='paC2' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#E3EAF4'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F4F1EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#paC2)'/><rect y='186' width='640' height='34' fill='#8F8A80'/><rect x='120' y='130' width='400' height='14' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='150' y='108' width='40' height='22' fill='#8B5A2B'/><rect x='230' y='108' width='40' height='22' fill='#8B5A2B'/><rect x='360' y='108' width='40' height='22' fill='#4A2511'/><rect x='450' y='108' width='40' height='22' fill='#4A2511'/><rect x='290' y='70' width='50' height='60' fill='#C9CED6'/><g transform='translate(70 100)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#1E499B'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#1E499B'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#F4F1EA'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#F4F1EA' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#F4F1EA' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><rect x='86' y='126' width='20' height='26' fill='#fff' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='20' y='20' width='260' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F7C948'/><text x='150' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Chocolate is made here…</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Douala, Mbah visits a cocoa processing factory for the school magazine.","contexte":"<p>Mbah writes: “Somebody grows the cocoa in the South Region. Somebody makes the chocolate here. People have exported the chocolate to Nigeria by people.” His teacher comments: “Too many ‘somebody’! Use the passive voice, and don't write ‘by people’.”</p>","documents":[{"t":"Two voices","html":"<p>In the active voice, the subject does the action. In the passive voice, the subject receives the action; the doer (agent) is introduced by <em>by</em> or left out.</p>"}],"question":"How do we form the passive voice, and when should we use it?","tache":"Form the passive in the main tenses, decide when to keep or remove the agent, then rewrite Mbah's article.","hypotheses":["The passive is just the active with by added at the end.","We must always mention the agent with by.","The passive is be (in the tense of the active verb) + past participle; we use it when the action matters more than the doer, and we drop the agent when it is unknown or obvious."]},"parties":[{"t":"Active and passive voices","html":"<div class='def'><b>Active voice</b>The subject does the action: <em><u>Workers</u> make chocolate.</em></div><div class='def'><b>Passive voice</b>The subject receives the action: <em><u>Chocolate</u> is made (by workers).</em> The object of the active sentence becomes the subject of the passive sentence.</div><p class='formule'>passive = be (same tense as the active verb) + past participle (+ by + agent)</p><div class='ex'><b>Example</b>Active: <em>Farmers grow cocoa in the South Region.</em> → Passive: <em>Cocoa is grown in the South Region (by farmers).</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Watch out!</b>Only verbs with an object can become passive: « The bus arrived » has no passive.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"From active to passive","legende":"The object moves to the front, the verb becomes be + past participle, and the subject becomes the agent (by…), often dropped.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Two columns: active and passive sentence' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Active → passive</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='164.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Active</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Workers</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>make</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>chocolate.</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ subject acts</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='475.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Passive</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Chocolate</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>is made</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>(by workers).</text><text x='336' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ subject receives</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>“Somebody grows the cocoa” tells us nothing about the doer: the important thing is the cocoa. The passive puts it first: “The cocoa <strong>is grown</strong> in the South Region.”</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","The passive is not just “by” added: the object becomes the subject and the verb becomes be + past participle."]]},"retenir":"Passive: object → subject; be + past participle; by + agent."},{"t":"The passive in the main tenses","verrou":true},{"t":"When to use the passive and the agent","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","quiz":[],"c":"1re A","rang":34,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"apc":{"module":"ENVIRONMENT, WELLBEING AND HEALTH","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about environment, wellbeing and health","situation":"Mbah writes: “Somebody grows the cocoa in the South Region. Somebody makes the chocolate here. People have exported the chocolate to Nigeria by people.” His teacher comments: “Too many ‘somebody’! Use the passive voice, and don't write ‘by people’.”","tache":"Form the passive in the main tenses, decide when to keep or remove the agent, then rewrite Mbah's article."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
/* ═══ FIN lot 6 anglais 3e (abonnés) ═══ */
/* ═══ AJOUT lot 7 anglais 1re-Tle (abonnés) (hors build principal : source à verser dans le dossier des sources) ═══ */
VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-used-to",{"titre":"Used to, didn't use to and be / get used to + -ing","duree":35,"famille":"Health and communication","agir":"Talk about past habits and about things that are familiar or becoming familiar","accroche":"“I used to fetch water from the stream.” “Now I am used to having a tap.” Two expressions, two meanings. Don't mix them up!","intro":"Mbi, a Lower Sixth student, moved from a village near Wum to Yaoundé. Talking about his old and new life will help you master used to and be used to.","objectifs":["use used to + base verb for past habits and states","form the negative and question with did","use be used to / get used to + noun or -ing","distinguish the two structures"],"enquete":{"titre":"From the village to the city","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Left: a village hut and a boy carrying a water pot on his head; right: city buildings, traffic and a tap' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='usC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#E6EEF7'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F4F1EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#usC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#B5834E'/><rect x='320' y='0' width='3' height='220' fill='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='60' y='120' width='90' height='56' fill='#B5652E'/><path d='M50 124L105 84L160 124Z' fill='#C9A04A'/><g transform='translate(220 88)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#2E7D32'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><ellipse cx='220' cy='80' rx='14' ry='10' fill='#8B4A2B'/><rect x='380' y='60' width='60' height='116' fill='#DCE6F2' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='450' y='30' width='60' height='146' fill='#DCE6F2' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='530' y='70' width='60' height='106' fill='#DCE6F2' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='600' y='130' width='4' height='46' fill='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='600' y='130' width='16' height='4' fill='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='20' y='20' width='230' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F7C948'/><text x='135' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>I used to… / I am used to…</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"Mbi compares his old life near Wum with his new life in Yaoundé.","contexte":"<p>Mbi writes to his English teacher: “In the village, I was used to fetch water every morning. Now I use to take a taxi to school. At first, I wasn't used to hear so much noise, but now I get used to it.” The teacher answers: “Nice story, but used to and be used to are mixed up!”</p>","documents":[{"t":"Two meanings","html":"<p>used to + verb = a past habit that no longer exists (« avant, j'allais… »). be used to + -ing = to be accustomed to something (« être habitué à »).</p>"}],"question":"How do we use used to and be used to correctly?","tache":"Learn the two structures, their forms and their meanings, then correct Mbi's letter.","hypotheses":["Used to and be used to mean the same thing.","Used to can be used for present habits: “I use to take a taxi”.","Used to + base verb = past habit; be / get used to + noun or -ing = be accustomed / become accustomed; for present habits we use the present simple."]},"parties":[{"t":"Used to + base verb: past habits","html":"<div class='def'><b>Used to</b>used to + base verb expresses a habit or a state in the past that is no longer true now.</div><p class='formule'>subject + used to + base verb</p><ul><li><em>I <strong>used to fetch</strong> water every morning.</em> (I don't anymore.)</li><li><em>There <strong>used to be</strong> no tarred road in our village.</em></li><li>Negative: <em>I <strong>didn't use to</strong> take taxis.</em></li><li>Question: <em><strong>Did</strong> you <strong>use to</strong> walk to school?</em></li></ul><div class='ex'><b>Mbi's past</b><em>When I lived near Wum, I used to wake up at 5 a.m. and I used to help my father on the farm.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Watch out!</b>There is no present form: for a present habit use the present simple — « I use to take a taxi » ✗ → <em>I usually take a taxi</em>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Then and now","legende":"Used to describes a finished past habit; the present simple describes the current habit.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Two columns: Mbi’s past habits and present habits' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Mbi's life</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#B5652E' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#B5652E'/><text x='164.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Then (used to)</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I used to fetch water</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I used to walk 5 km</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I didn't use to</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>take taxis</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='475.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Now (present simple)</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I have a tap</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I take a taxi</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I usually wake up</text><text x='336' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>at 6 a.m.</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>“I was used to fetch water” mixes the two structures. Mbi wants to talk about a past habit: “I <strong>used to fetch</strong> water every morning.” And for today: “Now I <strong>take</strong> a taxi”, not “I use to”.</p>","verdicts":[[1,"rejetee","Used to has no present form: use the present simple for present habits."]]},"retenir":"used to + base verb (past habit); didn't use to; did… use to?; no present form."},{"t":"Be used to / get used to + -ing","verrou":true},{"t":"Distinguishing the structures","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","quiz":[],"c":"1re A","rang":28,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"apc":{"module":"ENVIRONMENT, WELLBEING AND HEALTH","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about environment, wellbeing and health","situation":"Mbi writes to his English teacher: “In the village, I was used to fetch water every morning. Now I use to take a taxi to school. At first, I wasn't used to hear so much noise, but now I get used to it.” The teacher answers: “Nice story, but used to and be used to are mixed up!”","tache":"Learn the two structures, their forms and their meanings, then correct Mbi's letter."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
