VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-so-neither",{"titre":"Grammar: agreeing with so, neither, too and either","duree":30,"famille":"Economic life and occupations","agir":"Agree and disagree briefly in a conversation about money and spending, using short answers with auxiliaries","accroche":"In Bafoussam, Grace says: “I spend too much money on airtime.” Her cousin Paul answers: “Me too I spend.” Then Grace says: “I didn't save anything last month.” Paul: “So didn't I.” Their English teacher smiles. What should Paul say?","intro":"Grace and Paul, two cousins in Bafoussam, compare how they manage their pocket money. Their conversation will help you agree and disagree in short answers with so, neither, nor, too and either, choosing the right auxiliary.","objectifs":["agree with a positive statement: So + auxiliary + subject (So do I) or subject + auxiliary + too (I do too)","agree with a negative statement: Neither / Nor + auxiliary + subject (Neither did I) or subject + auxiliary + not + either (I didn't either)","choose the auxiliary that matches the tense of the first sentence (do, does, did, am, have, can, will…)","disagree with short answers: I do. / I don't. / I did. / I didn't."],"enquete":{"titre":"Two cousins and their pocket money","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Two cousins at a table with piggy banks and a notebook of expenses' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='snC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#FCE4EC'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#snC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#D7CCC8'/><rect x='380' y='130' width='220' height='14' fill='#8D6E63'/><ellipse cx='440' cy='118' rx='26' ry='16' fill='#F48FB1'/><ellipse cx='540' cy='118' rx='26' ry='16' fill='#90CAF9'/><g transform='translate(130 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><g transform='translate(220 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1E499B'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><rect x='20' y='20' width='260' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#F8BBD0'/><text x='150' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>I spend too much on airtime.</text><rect x='300' y='20' width='140' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#BBDEFB'/><text x='370' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>So do I.</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Bafoussam, Grace and Paul compare how they spend their pocket money.","contexte":"<p>Paul answers “Me too I spend” and “So didn't I”. His friend Thierry thinks: “In English, you just add <em>too</em> at the end, it's always correct.” Their teacher writes four sentences on the board and asks them to answer each one in three words. Grace and Paul each spend 500 FCFA a day on airtime and get 20 000 FCFA of pocket money a month.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The teacher's sentences","html":"<p>1. Grace spends too much on airtime. 2. Grace didn't save anything last month. 3. Grace has opened a mobile money savings account. 4. Grace can't stop buying snacks. — Answer as Paul, who does / did / has / can't the same.</p>"}],"question":"How do we agree and disagree in short answers with so, neither, too and either?","tache":"Learn the structures so / neither / too / either with auxiliaries, then write Paul's correct answers to the four sentences and complete their savings plan.","hypotheses":["We can always add “too” at the end: “Me too I spend.”","“So” works with every sentence, even negative ones: “So didn't I.”","We repeat the auxiliary of the first sentence, with so / too for positive sentences and neither / nor / either for negative ones."]},"parties":[{"t":"Agreeing with a positive statement: so and too","html":"<div class='def'><b>Short agreement</b>A short answer that says “the same is true for me” without repeating the whole sentence: So do I. / I do too. It uses the auxiliary of the first sentence.</div><ul><li><strong>So + auxiliary + subject</strong>: <em>I spend too much. — <strong>So do I.</strong></em></li><li><strong>Subject + auxiliary + too</strong>: <em>I spend too much. — <strong>I do too.</strong></em></li><li>The auxiliary matches the first verb: <em>Grace spends → So <strong>does</strong> Paul. Grace has opened → So <strong>has</strong> Paul. Grace can swim → So <strong>can</strong> Paul. Grace is tired → So <strong>am</strong> I.</em></li><li>With the simple present or past without auxiliary, use <strong>do / does / did</strong>.</li></ul><p class='formule'>positive statement → So + aux + subject / subject + aux + too</p><div class='ex'><b>Simple past → did</b><em>Grace: I spent all my money last week. — Paul: <strong>So did I.</strong> / <strong>I did too.</strong></em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>Inversion after <em>so</em>: <strong>So do I</strong>, not <s>So I do</s> (which means “Yes, it's true, I do”). And never <s>Me too I spend</s>: say <em>Me too</em> alone (informal) or <em>So do I</em>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Which auxiliary?","legende":"The auxiliary of the short answer is the one of the first sentence; if there is none, use do, does or did.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Four columns: the auxiliary to use in short answers' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>First sentence → short answer</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='86.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Simple present</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I spend…</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ So do I.</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>He spends…</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ So does she.</text><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='242.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Simple past</text><text x='180.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I saved…</text><text x='180.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ So did I.</text><text x='180.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>She bought…</text><text x='180.5' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ So did we.</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='397.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>be / have</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I'm broke.</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ So am I.</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I've saved.</text><text x='336' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ So have I.</text><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#7B3F99'/><text x='553.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Modals</text><text x='491.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I can save.</text><text x='491.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#7B3F99'>→ So can I.</text><text x='491.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I will try.</text><text x='491.5' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#7B3F99'>→ So will I.</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>“Me too I spend” mixes two structures and is not correct English. After a positive statement, we say <em>So do I</em>, <em>I do too</em> or, informally, <em>Me too</em> alone.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Adding too everywhere is wrong: use So + auxiliary + subject or subject + auxiliary + too."]]},"retenir":"So + aux + subject ; subject + aux + too ; same auxiliary and tense as the first sentence."},{"t":"Agreeing with a negative statement: neither, nor and either","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"Positive or negative statement?. So and too for positive statements; neither, nor and either for negative ones.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: positive statements, negative statements and errors' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Agreeing in short</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Positive (+)</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I like it.</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ So do I.</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ I do too.</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ Me too.</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Negative (−)</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I don't like it.</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ Neither do I.</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ I don't either.</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ Me neither.</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#7B3F99'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Watch out</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Neither did I ✓</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Neither didn't I ✗</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>So didn't I ✗</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#7B3F99'>→ one negation</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"Disagreeing and using short answers in context","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"1re A","rang":21,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Economic Life and Occupations","famille":"Vie économique","agir":"Communicate about economic life and occupations","situation":"In Bafoussam, Grace and Paul each spend 500 FCFA a day on airtime out of 20 000 FCFA of pocket money a month. When they compare, Paul answers “Me too I spend” and “So didn't I”, and their friend thinks adding “too” is always correct.","tache":"Learn the structures so / neither / too / either with auxiliaries, then write Paul's correct answers to the four sentences and complete their savings plan."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-partitives",{"titre":"Grammar: partitives — a bag of rice, a piece of advice","duree":30,"famille":"Economic life and occupations","agir":"Write and read shopping lists and recipes using partitives with uncountable and countable nouns","accroche":"Mama Nkeng runs a small restaurant in Bamenda. Her nephew writes her shopping list in English: “two rices, three oils, a bread, some bananas”. At the market, the trader laughs. How do we count things that cannot be counted?","intro":"Mama Nkeng's nephew prepares the shopping list for her restaurant in Bamenda. His list will help you learn partitives — a bag of, a bottle of, a bunch of, a piece of — to count uncountable nouns and groups of things.","objectifs":["distinguish countable and uncountable nouns (rice, oil, bread, advice, information)","use partitives: a bag of rice, a bottle of oil, a loaf of bread, a bunch of bananas, a piece of advice","make partitives plural: two bags of rice, three loaves of bread","use partitives in shopping lists, recipes and short texts"],"enquete":{"titre":"Mama Nkeng's shopping list","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A restaurant kitchen with a bag of rice, a bottle of oil, bananas and bread, and a boy with a list' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='ptC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#FFF8E1'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#ptC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#EFEBE9'/><rect x='360' y='120' width='250' height='14' fill='#8D6E63'/><rect x='370' y='72' width='50' height='48' fill='#FFF8E1' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='440' y='68' width='18' height='52' rx='4' fill='#FBC02D'/><ellipse cx='500' cy='108' rx='22' ry='10' fill='#FDD835'/><ellipse cx='570' cy='108' rx='26' ry='12' fill='#D7A86E'/><g transform='translate(130 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#C2540A'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><rect x='150' y='110' width='34' height='44' fill='#fff' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='20' y='20' width='280' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#FFE082'/><text x='160' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Two rices, three oils…?</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Bamenda, Mama Nkeng's nephew writes the shopping list for her restaurant.","contexte":"<p>The nephew writes: “two rices, three oils, a bread, some bananas, an advice for the cook”. His sister says: “Just add -s to every word, like in French.” Mama Nkeng needs exactly: 2 bags of rice of 25 kg, 3 bottles of oil of 5 litres, 6 loaves of bread, 4 bunches of plantains and 2 bars of soap. Prices: rice 17 500 a bag, oil 6 000 a bottle, bread 250 a loaf, plantains 2 000 a bunch, soap 300 a bar.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The nephew's first list","html":"<p>two rices · three oils · a bread · some bananas · two soaps · an advice for the cook: “don't put too much salt”</p>"}],"question":"How do we count uncountable nouns and groups of things in English?","tache":"Learn partitives and their plural, then rewrite the shopping list correctly and calculate its total cost.","hypotheses":["We can add -s to any noun: two rices, three oils.","“Some” is always enough; we never need to be precise.","Uncountable nouns are counted with a partitive (a bag of rice, a bottle of oil), and the partitive takes the plural (two bags of rice)."]},"parties":[{"t":"Countable and uncountable nouns","html":"<div class='def'><b>Partitive</b>An expression that shows a quantity or a part of something: a bag of, a bottle of, a loaf of, a piece of. It is used to count uncountable nouns or to name a group of things.</div><ul><li><strong>Countable nouns</strong> have a plural: <em>a banana, two bananas; a plantain, plantains</em>.</li><li><strong>Uncountable nouns</strong> have no plural and no <em>a / an</em>: <em>rice, oil, bread, water, salt, sugar, money, advice, information, news, furniture, luggage</em>.</li><li>To count them, use a <strong>partitive</strong>: <em>a bag of rice, a bottle of oil, a piece of advice</em>.</li></ul><p class='formule'>a / two + container or unit + of + uncountable noun</p><div class='ex'><b>Partitives in sentences</b><em>Can I have <strong>a cup of</strong> tea and <strong>a slice of</strong> bread, please? My father gave me <strong>a piece of</strong> advice.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>False friends: in French you say <em>des conseils, des informations, des meubles</em>; in English <strong>advice, information, furniture</strong> are uncountable: <s>two advices</s> → <em>two pieces of advice</em>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Countable or uncountable?","legende":"Uncountable nouns need a partitive to be counted.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: countable nouns, uncountable nouns and partitives' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Two kinds of nouns</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Countable</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a banana</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>two plantains</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>three eggs</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ a / -s</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Uncountable</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>rice, oil, bread</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>advice, news</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>information</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ no -s</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Partitive</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a bag of rice</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a bottle of oil</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a piece of advice</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ to count</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>“Two rices, three oils” is wrong: rice and oil are uncountable, they never take -s. The trader does not know whether the nephew wants two grains or two bags of rice!</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Uncountable nouns never take -s: use a partitive."]]},"retenir":"Uncountable: rice, oil, bread, advice, information, news, money ; no a / no -s ; count them with a partitive."},{"t":"The common partitives","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"Partitives by family. Containers, units, measures and groups.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Four columns: containers, units, measures and groups' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Common partitives</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='86.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Containers</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a bag of</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a bottle of</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a cup of</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a tin of</text><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='242.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Units</text><text x='180.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a loaf of</text><text x='180.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a slice of</text><text x='180.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a bar of</text><text x='180.5' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a sheet of</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='397.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Measures</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a kilo of</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a litre of</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a metre of</text><text x='336' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a spoonful of</text><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#7B3F99'/><text x='553.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Groups / abstract</text><text x='491.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a bunch of</text><text x='491.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a pair of</text><text x='491.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a piece of advice</text><text x='491.5' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a piece of news</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"The plural of partitives","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"1re A","rang":23,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Economic Life and Occupations","famille":"Vie économique","agir":"Communicate about economic life and occupations","situation":"In Bamenda, Mama Nkeng's nephew writes the restaurant's shopping list in English: “two rices, three oils, a bread, some bananas, an advice”. The trader laughs, and his sister thinks you can add -s to every word.","tache":"Learn partitives and their plural, then rewrite the shopping list correctly and calculate its total cost."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-compound-nouns",{"titre":"Grammar: compound nouns and their plurals","duree":30,"famille":"Environment, well-being and health","agir":"Use compound nouns correctly, with their plurals, in a text about health and prevention","accroche":"In Mbalmayo, the health club writes a poster: “Distribution of mosquitoes nets by the healths workers. Washs your hands at the hands-washing stations!” The nurse frowns. Where do the -s go in English compound nouns?","intro":"The health club of a school in Mbalmayo prepares a poster for a malaria and hygiene campaign. Their poster will help you learn how compound nouns are formed and how they make their plural.","objectifs":["recognise compound nouns: noun + noun (a mosquito net), adjective + noun (a blackboard), verb-ing + noun (a washing machine)","make the plural of compound nouns: only the main noun takes -s (mosquito nets, health workers)","know the special plurals: mothers-in-law, passers-by, women doctors","use compound adjectives with numbers without -s: a ten-day campaign, a five-litre bucket"],"enquete":{"titre":"The health club's poster","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A health centre with a red cross, a hand-washing station, boxes of mosquito nets and pupils with a poster' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='csC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#E8F5E9'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#csC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#DCEDC8'/><rect x='420' y='60' width='190' height='116' fill='#FAFAFA' stroke='#B0BEC5'/><rect x='505' y='78' width='20' height='6' fill='#C62828'/><rect x='512' y='71' width='6' height='20' fill='#C62828'/><rect x='300' y='120' width='40' height='56' fill='#1E88E5'/><g transform='translate(110 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><rect x='150' y='70' width='120' height='80' fill='#FFF8E1' stroke='#C9A04A'/><text x='210' y='100' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11' font-weight='700' fill='#C62828'>mosquitoes nets?</text><text x='210' y='124' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11' font-weight='700' fill='#C62828'>healths workers?</text><rect x='20' y='14' width='260' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#A5D6A7'/><text x='150' y='34' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Where does the -s go?</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Mbalmayo, the health club checks its poster before the campaign.","contexte":"<p>The club writes “mosquitoes nets”, “healths workers” and “a ten-days campaign”. One member says: “Put -s on every word, it's safer.” The nurse explains that in a compound noun, the first noun works like an adjective. The campaign will last 10 days; 4 health workers will give 3 mosquito nets to each of the 240 families of the neighbourhood.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The club's first poster","html":"<p>MALARIA AND HYGIENE CAMPAIGN · A ten-days campaign · Distribution of mosquitoes nets by the healths workers · Washs your hands at the hands-washing stations · Ask the nurses-in-chief for informations</p>"}],"question":"How do we form compound nouns and their plurals in English?","tache":"Learn how compound nouns are formed and how they make their plural, then correct the poster and calculate the number of mosquito nets.","hypotheses":["We put -s on every word of a compound noun to be safe.","Compound nouns never change in the plural.","Only the main noun (usually the last one) takes the plural; the first noun works like an adjective and stays singular."]},"parties":[{"t":"Forming compound nouns","html":"<div class='def'><b>Compound noun</b>A noun made of two or more words that together name one thing: a mosquito net, a health worker, a toothbrush, a mother-in-law. The main word (the head) is usually the last one.</div><ul><li><strong>Noun + noun</strong>: <em>a mosquito net, a health worker, a bus stop, a water tank, a football</em>.</li><li><strong>Adjective + noun</strong>: <em>a blackboard, a first-aid kit, a greenhouse</em>.</li><li><strong>Verb-ing + noun</strong> (use): <em>a washing machine, a swimming pool, a waiting room</em>.</li><li><strong>Three forms in writing</strong>: one word (<em>toothbrush</em>), two words (<em>health worker</em>), hyphen (<em>mother-in-law</em>).</li><li>The <strong>head</strong> is the last word: a <em>mosquito net</em> is a kind of <strong>net</strong>.</li></ul><p class='formule'>modifier (like an adjective, singular) + head noun (takes the plural)</p><div class='ex'><b>Finding the head</b><em>A <strong>health worker</strong> is a worker in health. A <strong>hand-washing station</strong> is a station for washing hands.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>The first noun stays singular even when the meaning is plural: <em>a <strong>tooth</strong>brush</em> (for many teeth), <em>a <strong>shoe</strong> shop</em>, <em>a <strong>hand</strong>-washing station</em>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Three ways to form compound nouns","legende":"The last word is the head; the first word describes it.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: noun plus noun, adjective plus noun, verb-ing plus noun' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Compound nouns</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Noun + noun</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>mosquito net</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>health worker</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>water tank</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ kind of net</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Adjective + noun</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>blackboard</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>first-aid kit</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>greenhouse</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ kind of board</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Verb-ing + noun</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>washing machine</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>waiting room</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>swimming pool</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ room for waiting</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>“Mosquitoes nets” and “healths workers” are wrong: the first noun works like an adjective, and English adjectives never take -s. Putting -s everywhere is not safer, it is wrong.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","The first noun is like an adjective: it never takes -s."]]},"retenir":"head noun = last word ; first noun = like an adjective, singular ; one word, two words or hyphen."},{"t":"The plural of compound nouns","verrou":true},{"t":"Compound adjectives with numbers","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"1re A","rang":36,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Environment, Well-Being and Health","famille":"Environnement et santé","agir":"Communicate about the environment, well-being and health","situation":"In Mbalmayo, the health club writes a poster: “A ten-days campaign · mosquitoes nets · healths workers · hands-washing stations”. One member wants to add -s to every word. The campaign will give 3 mosquito nets to each of 240 families with 4 health workers.","tache":"Learn how compound nouns are formed and how they make their plural, then correct the poster and calculate the number of mosquito nets."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-conjunctions",{"titre":"Grammar: conjunctions and linkers — although, despite, however, since, yet","duree":35,"famille":"Citizenship and human rights","agir":"Link ideas of contrast, cause and time correctly in a report about work culture and excellence","accroche":"In Garoua, the small garage of Mr Hamadou has won the town's “best workshop” prize. His apprentice Ali writes the report: “Despite the garage is small, but it won. However it has old tools, it works well.” His teacher circles every linker. Which ones are wrong?","intro":"Ali, an apprentice mechanic in Garoua, writes a report explaining why his small garage won a prize for excellence. His report will help you use conjunctions and linkers of contrast, cause and time: although, even though, despite, in spite of, however, yet, still, since, for.","objectifs":["express contrast with although / even though + clause and despite / in spite of + noun or -ing","use however, yet and still to link two sentences, with the right punctuation","express cause with since, as, for and time with since","avoid double linkers (although… but) and choose the right structure after each linker"],"enquete":{"titre":"The best workshop in Garoua","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A small garage with a trophy sign, a red car and two mechanics' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='gcC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#ECEFF1'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#gcC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#BDBDBD'/><rect x='380' y='50' width='230' height='126' fill='#ECEFF1' stroke='#78909C'/><rect x='430' y='64' width='130' height='26' rx='4' fill='#F9A825'/><text x='495' y='82' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>BEST WORKSHOP</text><rect x='410' y='130' width='120' height='30' rx='6' fill='#C62828'/><circle cx='430' cy='162' r='10' fill='#263238'/><circle cx='510' cy='162' r='10' fill='#263238'/><g transform='translate(130 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1565C0'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1565C0' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1565C0' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><g transform='translate(210 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#2E7D32'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><rect x='20' y='20' width='300' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#B0BEC5'/><text x='170' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Although the garage is small, it won.</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Garoua, the apprentice Ali writes the report on his garage's prize.","contexte":"<p>Ali writes: “Despite the garage is small, but it won. However it has old tools, it works well. Since three years, we never missed a deadline.” His friend says: “All these linkers mean the same thing; use any of them.” The garage repaired 480 cars last year, 96 % of them on time, with only 3 workers and old tools.</p>","documents":[{"t":"Ali's facts","html":"<p>The garage is small · old tools · only 3 workers · 480 cars repaired last year · 96 % on time · open since 2019 · always explains the price before working · the town council gave the prize because of punctuality, honesty and quality.</p>"}],"question":"How do we link ideas of contrast, cause and time correctly in English?","tache":"Learn the structures after although, despite, however, yet, since and for, then rewrite Ali's report correctly.","hypotheses":["All the linkers of contrast mean the same and can be used in the same way.","We can use two linkers together to be clearer: although… but.","Each linker has its own structure: although + clause, despite + noun or -ing, however between two sentences; and we use only one linker per link."]},"parties":[{"t":"Contrast inside a sentence: although, even though, despite, in spite of","html":"<div class='def'><b>Linker of contrast</b>A word or expression that shows that two facts are opposed or surprising together: although, even though, despite, in spite of, however, yet, still, whereas.</div><ul><li><strong>Although / even though + clause</strong> (subject + verb): <em><strong>Although</strong> the garage is small, it won the prize.</em></li><li><strong>Despite / in spite of + noun</strong>: <em><strong>Despite</strong> its old tools, the garage works well.</em></li><li><strong>Despite / in spite of + -ing</strong>: <em><strong>In spite of having</strong> only three workers, it repaired 480 cars.</em></li><li><strong>Despite the fact that + clause</strong>: <em>Despite the fact that the tools are old, …</em></li></ul><p class='formule'>although + subject + verb ; despite / in spite of + noun / verb-ing</p><div class='ex'><b>Even though: a stronger although</b><em><strong>Even though</strong> the garage has only three workers, it repaired 480 cars last year.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>Never <s>despite of</s>, never <s>despite the garage is small</s>. And never two linkers for one link: <s>Although it is small, but it won</s>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Clause or noun?","legende":"The linker decides what comes after it.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: linkers followed by a clause, a noun or a verb-ing' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Contrast in one sentence</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>+ clause</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>although it is small</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>even though it is old</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ subject + verb</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>+ noun</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>despite its size</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>in spite of the rain</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ a noun group</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>+ -ing</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>despite having</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>in spite of being</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ verb-ing</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>The linkers do not work in the same way: <em>despite</em> cannot be followed by a clause (“despite the garage is small”). Each linker has its own structure: although + clause, despite + noun or -ing.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Linkers of contrast have different structures."]]},"retenir":"although / even though + clause ; despite / in spite of + noun or -ing ; never despite of."},{"t":"Contrast between two sentences: however, yet, still","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"One link, one linker. Choose one linker of contrast, not two.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Two columns: wrong and correct uses of linkers' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Correct or wrong?</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='164.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Wrong</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Although…, but…</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Despite it is…</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>However it has…, it…</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ double / wrong</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='299' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='475.5' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Correct</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Although…, it won.</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Despite its size,…</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>…old. However, it…</text><text x='336' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ one linker</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"Cause and time: since, as, for","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"1re A","rang":41,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Citizenship and Human Rights","famille":"Citoyenneté","agir":"Communicate about citizenship and human rights","situation":"In Garoua, Mr Hamadou's small garage won the town's best workshop prize (480 cars repaired, 96 % on time, 3 workers, old tools). The apprentice Ali writes: “Despite the garage is small, but it won. However it has old tools, it works well. Since three years…”.","tache":"Learn the structures after although, despite, however, yet, since and for, then rewrite Ali's report correctly."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-each-other",{"titre":"Grammar: each, every, each other and one another","duree":30,"famille":"Citizenship and human rights","agir":"Talk about individual and shared responsibilities in a community using each, every, each other and one another","accroche":"In Nkongsamba, twelve young people clean their street every Saturday. Their report says: “Each members brings a broom. Every families give 500 francs. We help each others.” The neighbourhood chief reads it and smiles. Which words are wrong?","intro":"A youth group in Nkongsamba organises a cleaning day every Saturday. Their report will help you use each and every with singular nouns, and each other and one another to express reciprocal actions.","objectifs":["use each and every with a singular noun and a singular verb: each member brings…, every family gives…","distinguish each (individually, two or more) and every (all, three or more, as a group)","use each of + plural noun / pronoun: each of the members, each of us","express reciprocal actions with each other and one another: they help each other"],"enquete":{"titre":"Saturday cleaning in Nkongsamba","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='Young people cleaning a street with brooms and wheelbarrows in front of houses' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='ecC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#F1F8E9'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#ecC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#C5E1A5'/><rect x='0' y='150' width='640' height='26' fill='#9E9E9E'/><rect x='360' y='70' width='70' height='80' fill='#FFE0B2'/><rect x='450' y='70' width='70' height='80' fill='#E3F2FD'/><rect x='540' y='70' width='70' height='80' fill='#F8BBD0'/><g transform='translate(80 70)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1E499B'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><g transform='translate(150 70)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#C2540A'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><g transform='translate(220 70)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#6B4423'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/></g><g transform='translate(290 70)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#2E7D32'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><rect x='20' y='14' width='300' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C5E1A5'/><text x='170' y='34' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>We help each other every Saturday!</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Nkongsamba, twelve young people clean their street every Saturday.","contexte":"<p>The report says: “Each members brings a broom. Every families give 500 francs. We help each others. Each of member clean one gutter.” A friend says: “Each and every are the same, and they go with plural nouns because there are many people.” The group has 12 members; the 30 families of the street each give 500 FCFA a month for gloves and bags.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The group's facts","html":"<p>12 members · every Saturday, 7 a.m. to 10 a.m. · each member cleans one part of the gutter · 30 families give 500 FCFA each a month · the members help one another to carry the rubbish to the collection point · the chief thanks every member at the monthly meeting.</p>"}],"question":"How do we use each, every, each other and one another correctly?","tache":"Learn the rules of each, every, each of, each other and one another, then correct the report and calculate the group's monthly budget.","hypotheses":["Each and every go with plural nouns because they talk about many people.","Each and every always mean exactly the same thing.","Each and every take a singular noun and verb; each looks at people one by one, every at the whole group; each other and one another express reciprocal actions."]},"parties":[{"t":"Each and every + singular noun","html":"<div class='def'><b>Distributive</b>A word that looks at the members of a group: each considers them one by one, every considers all of them together. Both are followed by a singular noun and a singular verb.</div><ul><li><strong>Each + singular noun + singular verb</strong>: <em><strong>Each member brings</strong> a broom.</em></li><li><strong>Every + singular noun + singular verb</strong>: <em><strong>Every family gives</strong> 500 francs.</em></li><li><strong>Each</strong> = one by one, for two or more: <em>She has a broom in each hand.</em> (two hands → each, not every)</li><li><strong>Every</strong> = all, as a group, three or more; also for frequency: <em>every Saturday, every two weeks</em>.</li></ul><p class='formule'>each / every + singular noun + singular verb</p><div class='ex'><b>Each and every in one sentence</b><em><strong>Every</strong> Saturday, <strong>each</strong> member cleans one part of the gutter.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>Never <s>each members</s> or <s>every families</s>: the noun stays singular, and so does the verb: <em>every family <strong>gives</strong></em>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Each or every?","legende":"Each looks at the members one by one; every looks at the whole group.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns comparing each and every' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Each and every</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Each</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>one by one</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>2 or more</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>each hand</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ individually</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Every</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>all together</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>3 or more</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>every Saturday</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ the whole group</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Both</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>+ singular noun</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>+ singular verb</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>each member brings</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ grammar</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>The friend is wrong: even if many people are concerned, each and every are followed by a singular noun and a singular verb: “each member brings”, “every family gives”.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Each and every take a singular noun and a singular verb."]]},"retenir":"each / every + singular noun + singular verb ; each = one by one ; every = all, frequency."},{"t":"Each of, every one of, each other, one another","verrou":true},{"t":"Responsibilities: individual and shared","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"1re A","rang":44,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Citizenship and Human Rights","famille":"Citoyenneté","agir":"Communicate about citizenship and human rights","situation":"In Nkongsamba, a youth group of 12 members cleans the street every Saturday, with 500 FCFA a month from each of the 30 families. Their report says: “Each members brings a broom. Every families give 500 francs. We help each others.”","tache":"Learn the rules of each, every, each of, each other and one another, then correct the report and calculate the group's monthly budget."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-negative-adverbs",{"titre":"Grammar: negative adverbs and inversion — hardly, scarcely, never, seldom","duree":35,"famille":"Citizenship and human rights","agir":"Use negative adverbs and inversion to write a strong, formal report about a democratic and tolerant event","accroche":"In Kumba, after the school election debate, Comfort writes the report for the school magazine: “Never I have seen such a calm debate. Hardly the results were announced when everybody applauded.” Her teacher underlines both sentences. Why?","intro":"Comfort, a pupil in Kumba, writes a report on her school's election debate, a lesson in democracy and tolerance. Her report will help you use negative adverbs (hardly, scarcely, barely, never, seldom, rarely) and the inversion that follows them at the start of a sentence.","objectifs":["use negative adverbs in their normal position: I have never seen…, We hardly knew…","use inversion after a negative adverb at the start of a sentence: Never have I seen…","use the structures hardly / scarcely… when, no sooner… than, not only… but also","avoid double negatives: I hardly know (not I don't hardly know)"],"enquete":{"titre":"The election debate in Kumba","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A school hall with two candidates at lecterns, a ballot box and pupils listening' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='ngC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#E3F2FD'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#ngC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#D7CCC8'/><rect x='360' y='30' width='250' height='36' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='485' y='54' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>ELECTION DEBATE</text><rect x='380' y='110' width='40' height='66' fill='#8D6E63'/><rect x='540' y='110' width='40' height='66' fill='#8D6E63'/><rect x='460' y='130' width='44' height='46' fill='#E3F2FD' stroke='#1E499B'/><g transform='translate(400 40)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#C2540A'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><g transform='translate(560 40)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><g transform='translate(120 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#2E7D32'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><rect x='20' y='20' width='300' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#90CAF9'/><text x='170' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Never have I seen such a calm debate.</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Kumba, Comfort reports on the school election debate.","contexte":"<p>Comfort writes: “Never I have seen such a calm debate. Hardly the results were announced when everybody applauded. The candidates didn't hardly interrupt each other.” Her friend says: “Just put the adverb first; English word order doesn't change.” The debate lasted 90 minutes; 720 of the 800 pupils voted, and the winner had 396 votes.</p>","documents":[{"t":"Comfort's notes","html":"<p>two candidates, Eric and Joy · 90 minutes · no insults, no interruptions · questions from the pupils · results at 4 p.m.: Joy 396, Eric 324 · Eric congratulated Joy immediately · everybody applauded · a lesson in democracy and tolerance.</p>"}],"question":"How do we use negative adverbs, and when do we invert the subject and the auxiliary?","tache":"Learn the negative adverbs and the inversion after them, then rewrite Comfort's report correctly and calculate the turnout and the results.","hypotheses":["We can put the adverb first without changing anything: “Never I have seen…”.","Adding “not” makes the negation stronger: “didn't hardly”.","A negative adverb at the start of a sentence is followed by an inversion (auxiliary + subject), and negative adverbs never take a second negation."]},"parties":[{"t":"Negative adverbs in their normal position","html":"<div class='def'><b>Negative adverb</b>An adverb with a negative or nearly negative meaning: never, seldom, rarely (not often), hardly, scarcely, barely (almost not). It already contains the negation.</div><ul><li><strong>Position</strong>: before the main verb, after the auxiliary or be: <em>The candidates <strong>hardly</strong> interrupted each other. I have <strong>never</strong> seen such a debate. We <strong>seldom</strong> have calm debates.</em></li><li><strong>Meaning</strong>: <em>hardly / scarcely / barely</em> = almost not; <em>seldom / rarely</em> = not often; <em>never</em> = not at any time.</li><li><strong>No double negative</strong>: <em>They <strong>hardly</strong> interrupted</em>, not <s>They didn't hardly interrupt</s>.</li><li><strong>Hardly ≠ hard</strong>: <em>He works hard</em> (a lot) / <em>He hardly works</em> (almost not).</li></ul><p class='formule'>subject + (auxiliary) + negative adverb + main verb</p><div class='ex'><b>Normal position</b><em>Eric and Joy <strong>scarcely</strong> raised their voices. Such calm is <strong>rarely</strong> seen in a debate.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>These adverbs are already negative: never add <em>not</em> or <em>no</em>. <s>I didn't never see</s> → <em>I never saw</em>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Meaning of negative adverbs","legende":"Three groups: never, not often, almost not.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: never, seldom and hardly' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Negative adverbs</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Not at any time</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>never</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I have never seen…</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ 0 %</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Not often</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>seldom, rarely</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>We seldom see…</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ a few times</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Almost not</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>hardly, scarcely</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>barely</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>They hardly spoke.</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ very little</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>“Didn't hardly” is a double negative: hardly is already negative. Adding “not” does not make it stronger, it makes it wrong. Comfort must write “The candidates hardly interrupted each other.”</p>","verdicts":[[1,"rejetee","Negative adverbs are already negative: no second negation."]]},"retenir":"never, seldom, rarely, hardly, scarcely, barely ; before the main verb ; no double negative ; hard ≠ hardly."},{"t":"Inversion after a negative adverb","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"Normal order or inversion?. At the start of the sentence, the negative adverb brings the question order.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: normal order, inversion and errors' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Inversion</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Normal</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I have never seen…</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Candidates seldom…</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Eric not only…</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ subject first</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Emphatic</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Never have I seen…</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Seldom do candidates…</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Not only did Eric…</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ auxiliary first</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Wrong</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Never I have seen…</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Seldom candidates do…</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ no inversion</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"Hardly… when, no sooner… than","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"1re A","rang":47,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Citizenship and Human Rights","famille":"Citoyenneté","agir":"Communicate about citizenship and human rights","situation":"In Kumba, Comfort writes the school magazine report on a calm election debate (90 minutes, 720 voters out of 800, Joy 396 votes, Eric 324). She writes “Never I have seen…”, “Hardly the results were announced when…” and “didn't hardly interrupt”.","tache":"Learn the negative adverbs and the inversion after them, then rewrite Comfort's report correctly and calculate the turnout and the results."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
