VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-reading-personal-finances",{"titre":"Reading: managing personal finances","duree":35,"famille":"Economic life and occupations","agir":"Read an article about budgeting, find its main ideas and figures, and apply its advice to a personal budget","accroche":"In Ebolowa, Linda, 17, sells doughnuts after school and earns about 30 000 FCFA a month. At the end of every month, she has nothing left and does not know why. Her aunt gives her an article in English: “Make your money work for you”. Can reading it change her habits?","intro":"Linda, a pupil in Ebolowa who earns money by selling doughnuts, reads an article about managing personal finances. Her reading will help you learn the vocabulary of money and budgeting and the strategies to read an informative text: main ideas, details, figures and advice.","objectifs":["use the vocabulary of personal finances: income, expenses, budget, savings, needs, wants, debt, interest, mobile money","find the main idea of each paragraph and the writer's purpose","find and use the figures of a text (percentages, amounts) to answer questions","turn the advice of a text into a personal plan"],"enquete":{"titre":"Linda's empty purse","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A girl selling doughnuts and reading an article, with a bar chart of a budget' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='fiC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#FFF8E1'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#fiC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#D7CCC8'/><rect x='420' y='70' width='40' height='106' fill='#1E499B'/><rect x='480' y='134' width='40' height='42' fill='#2E7D32'/><rect x='540' y='110' width='40' height='66' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='440' y='64' text-anchor='middle' font-size='10' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>needs</text><text x='500' y='128' text-anchor='middle' font-size='10' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>savings</text><text x='560' y='104' text-anchor='middle' font-size='10' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>wants</text><g transform='translate(130 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><circle cx='200' cy='150' r='10' fill='#D7A86E'/><circle cx='222' cy='150' r='10' fill='#D7A86E'/><rect x='240' y='110' width='60' height='50' fill='#fff' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><rect x='20' y='20' width='300' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#FFE082'/><text x='170' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Pay yourself first: save before you spend.</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Ebolowa, Linda reads an article about budgeting to understand where her money goes.","contexte":"<p>Linda reads the article quickly, notices the word “debt” and decides that it does not concern her. Her friend says: “Budgets are for adults and companies; a pupil just spends.” Her aunt asks her to answer five questions on the article and to make her own budget. Linda earns about 30 000 FCFA a month.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The article: “Make your money work for you”","html":"<p>(1) Whether you earn 10 000 or 1 000 000 francs, the rule is the same: you must know where your money goes. Write down your income and every expense for one month. — (2) A simple method is the 50/30/20 rule: 50 % of your income for needs (food, transport, school materials), 30 % for wants (snacks, airtime, clothes you do not really need) and 20 % for savings. — (3) “Pay yourself first”: put your savings aside the day you receive your money, not at the end of the month. A mobile money savings account or a njangi can help. — (4) Avoid debt for things you want but do not need: borrowing 5 000 francs to buy a phone cover may cost you more if you have to pay interest. Small savings, kept regularly, grow into big projects.</p>"}],"question":"How do we read an article about personal finances and use its advice?","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of personal finances and the reading strategies, then answer the questions on the article and build Linda's monthly budget.","hypotheses":["Budgets are only for adults and companies.","Reading the article quickly and stopping at one word (debt) is enough.","We find the main idea of each paragraph, read the figures carefully, and apply the advice to a real budget."]},"parties":[{"t":"The vocabulary of personal finances","html":"<div class='def'><b>Budget</b>A plan that shows how much money you receive (income) and how you will use it (expenses and savings) over a period, usually a month.</div><ul><li><strong>Money in</strong>: <em>income, earnings, pocket money, a salary, profit</em>.</li><li><strong>Money out</strong>: <em>expenses, spending, bills, fees, a purchase</em>.</li><li><strong>Kinds of expenses</strong>: <em>needs</em> (necessary) and <em>wants</em> (pleasant but not necessary).</li><li><strong>Keeping money</strong>: <em>savings, to save, a savings account, a njangi, mobile money</em>.</li><li><strong>Borrowing</strong>: <em>a loan, to borrow, to lend, debt, interest</em>.</li></ul><p class='formule'>income − expenses = savings (or debt if negative)</p><div class='ex'><b>Words in context</b><em>My income is 30 000 francs a month. My needs cost 15 000, my wants 9 000, so I can save 6 000.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>“To borrow” = take money from someone; “to lend” = give money to someone for a time: <em>Can you lend me 500 francs? Can I borrow 500 francs?</em></div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Needs, wants and savings","legende":"Three kinds of uses for your money.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: needs, wants and savings' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Where does the money go?</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Needs</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>food, transport</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>school materials</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>rent, health</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ necessary</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Wants</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>snacks, airtime</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>new clothes</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>outings</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ pleasant</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Savings</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>savings account</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>njangi</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>mobile money</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ for the future</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>The friend is wrong: the article says the rule is the same “whether you earn 10 000 or 1 000 000 francs”. A pupil who earns 30 000 francs a month needs a budget as much as an adult.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Everybody who has money needs a budget, pupils too."]]},"retenir":"income, expenses, budget ; needs ≠ wants ; savings, njangi ; loan, debt, interest ; borrow ≠ lend."},{"t":"Reading for main ideas and details","verrou":true},{"t":"Applying the advice: Linda's budget","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"1re A","rang":20,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Economic Life and Occupations","famille":"Vie économique","agir":"Communicate about economic life and occupations","situation":"In Ebolowa, Linda, 17, earns about 30 000 FCFA a month selling doughnuts but has nothing left at the end of each month. She reads quickly an article on budgeting, stops at the word “debt”, and her friend thinks budgets are only for adults.","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of personal finances and the reading strategies, then answer the questions on the article and build Linda's monthly budget."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-reading-communicable-diseases",{"titre":"Reading: preventing communicable diseases","duree":35,"famille":"Environment, well-being and health","agir":"Read a health leaflet, identify how diseases spread and how to prevent them, and pass on the message","accroche":"In a village near Kousséri, three children have caught cholera after the rains. Some neighbours say it is a curse. Amina, a pupil in 1re, reads a health leaflet in English given by an NGO. What does it say, and how can she convince her neighbours?","intro":"Amina, a pupil near Kousséri, reads a leaflet on communicable diseases after a cholera outbreak in her village. Her reading will help you learn the vocabulary of diseases and prevention and the strategies to read a leaflet: headings, causes, symptoms, prevention and instructions.","objectifs":["use the vocabulary of communicable diseases: germ, infection, symptoms, to spread, contaminated water, vaccine, hygiene, outbreak","read a leaflet using its headings: how it spreads, symptoms, prevention, what to do","distinguish facts from beliefs and justify answers with the text","turn the leaflet's instructions into clear advice for others"],"enquete":{"titre":"Cholera after the rains","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A village with a well, a water tank with a tap, a latrine and a girl reading a health leaflet' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='chC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#E8F5E9'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#chC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#DCEDC8'/><ellipse cx='450' cy='160' rx='30' ry='10' fill='#90A4AE'/><rect x='420' y='130' width='60' height='30' fill='#90A4AE'/><rect x='520' y='100' width='50' height='76' fill='#A1887F'/><rect x='360' y='110' width='34' height='66' fill='#1E88E5'/><g transform='translate(130 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#C2540A'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><rect x='150' y='106' width='50' height='60' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32'/><text x='175' y='126' text-anchor='middle' font-size='9' font-weight='700' fill='#2E7D32'>HEALTH</text><rect x='20' y='20' width='300' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#A5D6A7'/><text x='170' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Cholera spreads through dirty water.</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"Near Kousséri, Amina reads a health leaflet after a cholera outbreak.","contexte":"<p>Some neighbours say the disease is a curse; others say only the sick must be careful. Amina reads the leaflet once and remembers only “wash your hands”. The NGO asks pupils to explain the leaflet to their families. In the village, 120 families use the same well; the NGO gives each family a 20-litre jerrycan and chlorine tablets.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The leaflet: “Stop cholera”","html":"<p><strong>What is cholera?</strong> A disease caused by a germ found in water or food contaminated by faeces. <strong>How does it spread?</strong> By drinking dirty water, eating unwashed food, and through dirty hands. It spreads fast during the rainy season. <strong>Symptoms</strong>: sudden watery diarrhoea, vomiting, rapid loss of water from the body. <strong>Prevention</strong>: drink boiled or treated water; wash your hands with soap before eating and after using the toilet; cover water containers; use latrines; wash fruit and vegetables. <strong>What to do</strong>: give oral rehydration solution (ORS) and go to the health centre immediately.</p>"}],"question":"How do we read a health leaflet and use it to prevent communicable diseases?","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of communicable diseases and the reading strategies, then answer the questions on the leaflet and write the advice Amina will give her neighbours.","hypotheses":["The disease is a curse: reading a leaflet will not help.","Remembering one instruction (wash your hands) is enough.","We read each heading (cause, spread, symptoms, prevention, what to do), separate facts from beliefs, and pass on all the instructions."]},"parties":[{"t":"The vocabulary of communicable diseases","html":"<div class='def'><b>Communicable disease</b>A disease that can pass from one person to another, or from an animal or the environment to people, through germs: cholera, typhoid, tuberculosis, measles, malaria (through mosquitoes).</div><ul><li><strong>Causes</strong>: <em>a germ, a virus, bacteria, a parasite, contaminated water, faeces, a mosquito bite</em>.</li><li><strong>Spread</strong>: <em>to spread, to infect, to be contagious, an outbreak, an epidemic</em>.</li><li><strong>Symptoms</strong>: <em>fever, diarrhoea, vomiting, a cough, dehydration</em>.</li><li><strong>Prevention</strong>: <em>hygiene, to boil, to treat water, soap, a latrine, a vaccine, to vaccinate, a mosquito net</em>.</li><li><strong>Treatment</strong>: <em>oral rehydration solution (ORS), a health centre, a nurse</em>.</li></ul><p class='formule'>germ → spread (water, food, hands) → symptoms → prevention / treatment</p><div class='ex'><b>Words in context</b><em>Cholera is caused by a germ in contaminated water. It spreads fast during the rainy season, when latrines overflow.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>“Disease” (maladie) is different from “decease” (décès). And “to catch a disease” = to get it: <em>Three children caught cholera.</em></div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"How cholera spreads and how to stop it","legende":"The same paths that spread the germ are the ones we can block.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: how cholera spreads, symptoms and prevention' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Cholera</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>It spreads by</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>dirty water</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>unwashed food</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>dirty hands</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C62828'>→ germ</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Symptoms</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>watery diarrhoea</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>vomiting</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>dehydration</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ danger</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Prevention</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>boil or treat water</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>wash hands with soap</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>use latrines</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ block it</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>The leaflet gives a clear cause: a germ in water or food contaminated by faeces. It is a fact that can be checked, not a curse; and because we know how it spreads, we can stop it.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Cholera is caused by a germ: a fact, not a curse."]]},"retenir":"germ, contaminated, to spread, outbreak ; symptoms: diarrhoea, vomiting, dehydration ; prevention: boil, wash, latrine, vaccine."},{"t":"Reading a leaflet with its headings","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"The plan of the leaflet. Five headings, five questions.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Five columns: the headings of the leaflet' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>“Stop cholera”</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='112.4' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='112.4' height='34' rx='11' fill='#7B3F99'/><text x='71.2' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>What?</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a germ</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>contaminated</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>water, food</text><rect x='139.4' y='44' width='112.4' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='139.4' y='44' width='112.4' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C62828'/><text x='195.60000000000002' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>How?</text><text x='149.4' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>dirty water</text><text x='149.4' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>dirty hands</text><text x='149.4' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>rainy season</text><rect x='263.8' y='44' width='112.4' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='263.8' y='44' width='112.4' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Symptoms</text><text x='273.8' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>diarrhoea</text><text x='273.8' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>vomiting</text><text x='273.8' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>water loss</text><rect x='388.20000000000005' y='44' width='112.4' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='388.20000000000005' y='44' width='112.4' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='444.40000000000003' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Prevention</text><text x='398.20000000000005' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>5 instructions</text><text x='398.20000000000005' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>boil, wash</text><text x='398.20000000000005' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>cover, latrines</text><rect x='512.6' y='44' width='112.4' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='512.6' y='44' width='112.4' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='568.8000000000001' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>What to do</text><text x='522.6' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>ORS</text><text x='522.6' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>health centre</text><text x='522.6' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>immediately</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"Passing on the message","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"1re A","rang":33,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Environment, Well-Being and Health","famille":"Environnement et santé","agir":"Communicate about the environment, well-being and health","situation":"Near Kousséri, three children caught cholera after the rains; some neighbours say it is a curse. Amina reads an NGO leaflet in English once and remembers only “wash your hands”. 120 families use the same well.","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of communicable diseases and the reading strategies, then answer the questions on the leaflet and write the advice Amina will give her neighbours."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-used-for-with",{"titre":"Grammar: used for, used in + -ing, used with + noun","duree":30,"famille":"Media and communication","agir":"Describe the use of tools, gadgets and media correctly with used for, used in, used with and used to","accroche":"In Dschang, Bertrand prepares a presentation on modern media for his class: “A USB flash drive is used for store files. A projector is used with to show slides.” His teacher circles “used for store” and “used with to show”. What is the right form?","intro":"Bertrand, a pupil in Dschang, prepares a presentation on the tools of modern media. His sentences will help you describe what objects are used for, in what activities and with what other objects — and avoid confusing these forms with “used to”.","objectifs":["describe the purpose of an object: be used for + verb-ing / be used to + base verb","describe the activity or field: be used in + noun / verb-ing","describe the object or person it goes with: be used with + noun","distinguish be used for / used to do, used to (past habit) and be used to + -ing (habit)"],"enquete":{"titre":"Bertrand's presentation on media tools","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A table with a phone, a USB flash drive, a laptop and a solar lamp, and a boy presenting' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='ufC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#E3F2FD'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#ufC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#D7CCC8'/><rect x='360' y='130' width='250' height='12' fill='#8D6E63'/><rect x='380' y='112' width='14' height='22' rx='3' fill='#263238'/><rect x='410' y='120' width='22' height='8' fill='#1E88E5'/><rect x='460' y='90' width='70' height='42' fill='#90CAF9' stroke='#455A64' stroke-width='4'/><rect x='560' y='104' width='16' height='28' fill='#F9A825'/><g transform='translate(130 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#2E7D32'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><rect x='20' y='20' width='300' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#90CAF9'/><text x='170' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>A flash drive is used for storing files.</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Dschang, Bertrand prepares a presentation on modern media tools.","contexte":"<p>Bertrand writes: “A USB flash drive is used for store files. A projector is used with to show slides. I am used to play games on my phone.” His friend says: “Used for, used to, used with — they are all the same.” His presentation has 6 slides; he speaks 2 minutes per slide.</p>","documents":[{"t":"Bertrand's notes","html":"<p>USB flash drive: storing and carrying files · projector: showing slides, with a laptop · smartphone: calling, taking photos, used in journalism · solar lamp: lighting, used with a solar panel · microphone: speaking to a big audience.</p>"}],"question":"How do we describe what objects are used for, in and with?","tache":"Learn the forms used for / used to / used in / used with and the different meanings of “used to”, then correct Bertrand's sentences and complete his presentation.","hypotheses":["Used for, used in, used with and used to are all the same.","After “used for”, we put the base verb: “used for store”.","Used for + verb-ing (purpose), used in + activity, used with + noun; and “used to” changes meaning according to the verb before it."]},"parties":[{"t":"Used for + -ing: the purpose","html":"<div class='def'><b>Passive of use</b>The structure be used + preposition describes what an object is for (used for), in what activity (used in) or with what (used with). It is a passive: the object is used by people.</div><ul><li><strong>be used for + verb-ing</strong>: <em>A USB flash drive is used for <strong>storing</strong> files.</em></li><li><strong>be used to + base verb</strong> (same meaning): <em>A USB flash drive is used to <strong>store</strong> files.</em></li><li><strong>be used for + noun</strong>: <em>A projector is used for <strong>presentations</strong>.</em></li><li>Question: <em>What is it used for?</em></li></ul><p class='formule'>be used for + verb-ing / noun = be used to + base verb</p><div class='ex'><b>Two correct forms</b><em>What is a solar lamp used for? — It is used for lighting houses without electricity. / It is used to light houses…</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>After a preposition (for, in, with), a verb takes -ing: <s>used for store</s> → <em>used for storing</em>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Two ways to say the purpose","legende":"for + -ing, or to + base verb: same meaning.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: used for plus -ing, used to plus verb, used for plus noun' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>What is it used for?</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>used for + -ing</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>for storing files</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>for showing slides</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>for lighting</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ preposition</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>used to + verb</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>to store files</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>to show slides</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>to light</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ infinitive</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>used for + noun</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>for presentations</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>for calls</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>for lighting</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ a noun</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>“Used for store” is wrong: “for” is a preposition and must be followed by a noun or a verb-ing. Bertrand must write “used for storing files” or “used to store files”.</p>","verdicts":[[1,"rejetee","After for, the verb takes -ing: used for storing."]]},"retenir":"be used for + -ing / noun ; be used to + base verb ; What is it used for?"},{"t":"Used in and used with","verrou":true},{"t":"Three meanings of “used to”","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"1re A","rang":54,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Media and Communication","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about media and communication","situation":"In Dschang, Bertrand prepares a 6-slide presentation on modern media tools and writes “A USB flash drive is used for store files”, “A projector is used with to show slides” and “I am used to play games”; his friend thinks all these forms are the same.","tache":"Learn the forms used for / used to / used in / used with and the different meanings of “used to”, then correct Bertrand's sentences and complete his presentation."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-listening-icts",{"titre":"Listening: using the new information and communication technologies","duree":35,"famille":"Media and communication","agir":"Listen to a talk about ICT tools, note the uses, advantages and risks of each one, and give advice for safe use","accroche":"In Bertoua, the school's new cyber-corner opens. The IT teacher gives a talk in English on the radio club: WhatsApp, the web, MP3, USB drives, e-mail… Kevin hears “USB… virus… password” and concludes: “ICTs are dangerous, I won't use them.” Has he understood the talk?","intro":"Kevin, a pupil in Bertoua, listens to a talk about the new information and communication technologies (ICTs) at the opening of his school's cyber-corner. His listening will help you learn the vocabulary of ICTs and the strategies to note uses, advantages and risks, and to give advice for safe use.","objectifs":["use the vocabulary of ICTs: the web, a website, a browser, e-mail, an attachment, WhatsApp, an MP3 file, a USB flash drive, a password, a virus, to download, to upload","listen to a talk and note, for each tool, its use, an advantage and a risk","recognise the speaker's signposts: first, another tool is, on the other hand, finally","give advice for safe and useful use: Never share…, Always scan…, You'd better…"],"enquete":{"titre":"The cyber-corner talk","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A school cyber-corner with computers, a router and pupils listening to a teacher' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='icC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#E3F2FD'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#icC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#ECEFF1'/><rect x='380' y='96' width='60' height='40' fill='#263238'/><rect x='384' y='100' width='52' height='32' fill='#42A5F5'/><rect x='374' y='140' width='72' height='8' fill='#8D6E63'/><rect x='460' y='96' width='60' height='40' fill='#263238'/><rect x='464' y='100' width='52' height='32' fill='#42A5F5'/><rect x='454' y='140' width='72' height='8' fill='#8D6E63'/><rect x='540' y='96' width='60' height='40' fill='#263238'/><rect x='544' y='100' width='52' height='32' fill='#42A5F5'/><rect x='534' y='140' width='72' height='8' fill='#8D6E63'/><g transform='translate(110 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#C2540A'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><g transform='translate(180 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><g transform='translate(260 80)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1E499B'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#6B4423'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#6B4423'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#6B4423'/></g><rect x='20' y='20' width='330' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#90CAF9'/><text x='185' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Always scan a USB drive before opening it.</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Bertoua, the IT teacher presents the tools of the new cyber-corner.","contexte":"<p>Kevin notes only the frightening words and decides not to use ICTs. His friend Clara says: “I just copy what the teacher says, word for word.” She gives up after one minute. The club asks for a table: tool · use · advantage · risk · advice. The cyber-corner has 12 computers; each class can use it 2 hours a week.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The talk (transcript)","html":"<p>“Good morning! First, the web: you use a browser to visit websites and find information for your homework. The advantage is speed; the risk is false information, so always check two sources. Another tool is e-mail: you can send a letter with an attachment, like your CV. Never open an attachment from someone you don't know. Then WhatsApp: it's free with data and great for class groups, but think before you share photos — once they're online, you can't take them back. MP3 files let you listen to lessons and music offline. Finally, USB flash drives carry your files, but they can carry viruses too: always scan them before opening. And remember: a strong password has at least eight characters — letters, numbers and symbols — and you never share it.”</p>"}],"question":"How do we listen to a talk about ICTs and note their uses, advantages and risks?","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of ICTs and the listening strategies, then complete the club's table and write three pieces of advice for safe use.","hypotheses":["ICTs are dangerous: it is better not to use them.","We must write the talk word for word.","We prepare a table, listen for each tool after the signposts, note use, advantage and risk in key words, then give balanced advice."]},"parties":[{"t":"The vocabulary of ICTs","html":"<div class='def'><b>ICTs</b>Information and communication technologies: the tools used to create, store, find and share information — computers, phones, the internet, e-mail, social media, digital files.</div><ul><li><strong>The internet</strong>: <em>the web, a website, a browser, a search engine, to browse, to search, online / offline</em>.</li><li><strong>Communication</strong>: <em>e-mail, an attachment, WhatsApp, a group, a voice note, a video call</em>.</li><li><strong>Files and storage</strong>: <em>a file, a folder, an MP3, a PDF, a USB flash (pen) drive, to download, to upload, to save</em>.</li><li><strong>Security</strong>: <em>a password, a virus, an antivirus, to scan, a scam, privacy, to hack</em>.</li></ul><p class='formule'>tool → use → advantage → risk → advice</p><div class='ex'><b>Words in context</b><em>I downloaded the PDF of the lesson, saved it on my USB drive and sent it as an attachment to my friend.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>“To download” = to bring a file from the internet to your device; “to upload” = to send a file from your device to the internet.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Download or upload?","legende":"The direction of the file decides the verb.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: download, upload and save' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Moving files</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Download</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>internet → phone</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a PDF lesson</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>an MP3</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ bring down</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Upload</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>phone → internet</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>a photo</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>your CV</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ send up</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Save</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>keep a copy</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>on a USB drive</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>in a folder</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ store</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>The talk does not say that ICTs are dangerous: it gives an advantage and a risk for each tool, and advice to reduce the risk. Kevin noted only the risks, so he misunderstood the speaker's balanced message.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","The talk is balanced: advantages, risks and advice."]]},"retenir":"web, browser, website ; e-mail, attachment ; file, MP3, USB drive ; download ≠ upload ; password, virus, scan."},{"t":"Taking notes with signposts","verrou":true},{"t":"Giving advice for safe use","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"1re A","rang":56,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Media and Communication","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about media and communication","situation":"In Bertoua, the IT teacher presents the tools of the new cyber-corner (web, e-mail, WhatsApp, MP3, USB drives). Kevin notes only “virus” and “password” and decides ICTs are dangerous, and Clara tries to write every word and gives up.","tache":"Learn the vocabulary of ICTs and the listening strategies, then complete the club's table and write three pieces of advice for safe use."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-how-questions",{"titre":"Grammar: “How” questions — how much, how many, how long, how often…","duree":30,"famille":"Media and communication","agir":"Ask precise questions with how + adjective / adverb / much / many to interview someone for the media","accroche":"In Limbe, the school radio interviews a famous Cameroonian athlete. Grace has prepared her questions: “How many money did you win? How long you train every day? How far is it the stadium?” The athlete smiles politely. What went wrong?","intro":"Grace, a pupil in Limbe, prepares an interview for her school radio. Her questions will help you form “how” questions correctly: how much and how many, how long, how often, how far, how old, how + adjective, and the word order after them.","objectifs":["use how much (uncountable) and how many (countable) correctly","ask about time, frequency, distance, age and size: how long, how often, how far, how old, how tall / big","respect the question word order: How + word + auxiliary + subject + verb?","use indirect “how” questions politely: Could you tell me how long you train?"],"enquete":{"titre":"The radio interview","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A school radio studio with two microphones, a journalist and an athlete' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='hwC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#FFEBEE'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#hwC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#D7CCC8'/><rect x='380' y='34' width='230' height='30' fill='#C62828'/><text x='495' y='54' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>ON AIR — RADIO LIMBE</text><rect x='360' y='136' width='260' height='12' fill='#455A64'/><rect x='420' y='110' width='3' height='26' fill='#B0BEC5'/><circle cx='421' cy='106' r='7' fill='#263238'/><rect x='550' y='110' width='3' height='26' fill='#B0BEC5'/><circle cx='551' cy='106' r='7' fill='#263238'/><g transform='translate(130 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#7B3F99'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#5A3A1E'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#5A3A1E'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#5A3A1E'/></g><g transform='translate(220 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#2E7D32'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><rect x='20' y='20' width='300' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#EF9A9A'/><text x='170' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>How often do you train?</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Limbe, Grace interviews an athlete for the school radio.","contexte":"<p>Grace's questions: “How many money did you win? How long you train every day? How far is it the stadium? How much races did you run?” Her co-host says: “How much and how many are the same, and word order doesn't matter in a question.” The athlete trains 3 hours a day, 6 days a week, runs 12 km every morning, and ran 25 races last season.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The athlete's facts","html":"<p>age: 24 · height: 1.78 m · trains 3 hours a day, 6 days a week · runs 12 km every morning · the stadium is 4 km from home · 25 races last season, 9 victories · prize money: 2 500 000 FCFA.</p>"}],"question":"How do we form “how” questions correctly in English?","tache":"Learn the “how” questions and their word order, then rewrite Grace's interview questions and calculate the athlete's weekly training.","hypotheses":["How much and how many are the same.","Word order does not matter in a question: “How long you train?”","How much goes with uncountable nouns and how many with countable ones; after how + word comes the question order: auxiliary + subject + verb."]},"parties":[{"t":"How much and how many","html":"<div class='def'><b>“How” question</b>A question that starts with how, alone (manner: How do you train?) or followed by an adjective, an adverb, much or many, to ask about quantity, time, distance, frequency, age or size.</div><ul><li><strong>How many + plural countable noun</strong>: <em>How many <strong>races</strong> did you run? How many <strong>victories</strong>?</em></li><li><strong>How much + uncountable noun</strong>: <em>How much <strong>money</strong> did you win? How much <strong>time</strong> do you spend…?</em></li><li><strong>How much</strong> alone = price: <em>How much are your running shoes?</em></li><li><strong>How</strong> alone = manner: <em>How do you prepare for a race?</em></li></ul><p class='formule'>How many + plural noun ; How much + uncountable noun ; How much…? = price</p><div class='ex'><b>Countable and uncountable</b><em>How many races did you run last season? — Twenty-five. How much prize money did you win? — Two and a half million francs.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>Money, time, water, information are uncountable: <em>how <strong>much</strong> money</em>, never <s>how many money</s>.</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"How much or how many?","legende":"Countable nouns take many; uncountable nouns take much.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: how many, how much and how much as price' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Quantity questions</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>How many</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>+ plural noun</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>races, victories</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>kilometres, days</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ countable</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>How much</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>+ uncountable noun</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>money, time</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>water, training</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ uncountable</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>How much?</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>alone</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>= the price</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>How much is it?</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ cost</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>How much and how many are not the same: “money” is uncountable (how much money), “races” is countable (how many races). Grace mixed them twice.</p>","verdicts":[[0,"rejetee","Much + uncountable, many + countable: they are not the same."]]},"retenir":"How many + plural countable ; How much + uncountable ; How much is it? = price ; How do you…? = manner."},{"t":"How long, how often, how far, how old…","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"Which “how” for which answer?. The expected answer tells you which word to use after how.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Four columns: how long, how often, how far and how old' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Asking with how</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='86.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>how long</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>duration</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>3 hours</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ time</text><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='242.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>how often</text><text x='180.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>frequency</text><text x='180.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>6 days a week</text><text x='180.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ times</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='397.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>how far</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>distance</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>4 km</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ space</text><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#7B3F99'/><text x='553.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>how old / tall</text><text x='491.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>age, height</text><text x='491.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>24, 1.78 m</text><text x='491.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#7B3F99'>→ person</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"Indirect “how” questions","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"1re A","rang":57,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Media and Communication","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about media and communication","situation":"In Limbe, Grace prepares an interview for the school radio with an athlete (24 years old, 3 hours a day, 6 days a week, 12 km every morning, 25 races, 9 victories). Her questions are “How many money…? How long you train…? How far is it the stadium?”","tache":"Learn the “how” questions and their word order, then rewrite Grace's interview questions and calculate the athlete's weekly training."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
VRT_L("1re-a-anglais-preferences-punctuation",{"titre":"Grammar: expressing preferences and using punctuation","duree":35,"famille":"Media and communication","agir":"Express and compare preferences correctly and punctuate a short opinion text about media","accroche":"In Maroua, the school blog asks: “Radio or social media: which do you prefer for news?” Ali writes: “i prefer the radio than social media because its more reliable i would rather to listen the news at 7 am” His teacher sends it back covered in red ink. What's wrong?","intro":"Ali, a pupil in Maroua, writes a comment on his school blog about how he prefers to get the news. His comment will help you express preferences correctly — prefer… to, would rather… than, would prefer to — and punctuate a text: capital letters, full stops, commas, apostrophes and question marks.","objectifs":["use prefer + noun / -ing + to: I prefer the radio to social media","use would rather + base verb + than and would prefer + to-infinitive","use like… better than, my favourite…, I'd rather not…","punctuate correctly: capital letters, full stops, commas, apostrophes (it's / its), question marks"],"enquete":{"titre":"Ali's comment on the school blog","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 220' role='img' aria-label='A school blog page on a screen with a comment full of red corrections, a radio and a phone' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='220' fill='#fff'/><defs><linearGradient id='prC' x1='0' y1='0' x2='0' y2='1'><stop offset='0.00' stop-color='#F1F8E9'/><stop offset='1.00' stop-color='#F7F3EA'/></linearGradient></defs><rect width='640' height='220' fill='url(#prC)'/><rect y='176' width='640' height='44' fill='#DCEDC8'/><rect x='340' y='30' width='270' height='140' rx='8' fill='#FAFAFA' stroke='#9AA3AF'/><text x='475' y='56' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Radio or social media?</text><path d='M360 80H590M360 100H590M360 120H560' stroke='#C62828' stroke-width='2' stroke-dasharray='6 4'/><g transform='translate(130 92)'><ellipse cx='0' cy='84' rx='18' ry='4' fill='#001136' opacity='.18'/><rect x='-9' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><rect x='1' y='44' width='8' height='36' rx='3' fill='#2E3445'/><ellipse cx='-6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><ellipse cx='6' cy='81' rx='7' ry='3.5' fill='#1F2328'/><path d='M-13 46L-16 18C-16 13 -12 11 -6 10H6C12 11 16 13 16 18L13 46Z' fill='#1E499B'/><path d='M-15 16L-20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><path d='M15 16L20 40' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='7' stroke-linecap='round'/><circle cx='-20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><circle cx='20' cy='42' r='3.6' fill='#4A2E1A'/><rect x='-3.5' y='5' width='7' height='7' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='0' cy='-2' rx='9' ry='10.5' fill='#4A2E1A'/><path d='M-9 -4C-10 -14 -4 -13.5 0 -13.5S10 -14 9 -4C7 -9 -7 -9 -9 -4Z' fill='#1B1410'/><ellipse cx='-9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/><ellipse cx='9' cy='-1' rx='1.8' ry='3' fill='#4A2E1A'/></g><rect x='210' y='136' width='50' height='30' rx='4' fill='#263238'/><circle cx='225' cy='151' r='8' fill='#FFB74D'/><rect x='20' y='20' width='290' height='30' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C5E1A5'/><text x='165' y='40' text-anchor='middle' font-size='11.5' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>I prefer the radio to social media.</text><text x='634' y='215' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>","legende":"In Maroua, Ali's blog comment comes back covered in corrections.","contexte":"<p>Ali writes: “i prefer the radio than social media because its more reliable i would rather to listen the news at 7 am”. His friend says: “Punctuation is not important on the internet; people understand.” The blog's survey: of 250 pupils who answered, 140 prefer social media, 75 the radio and 35 television.</p>","documents":[{"t":"The blog question and survey","html":"<p><strong>Question of the week</strong>: Radio or social media: which do you prefer for news? Why? — <strong>Results (250 pupils)</strong>: social media 140 · radio 75 · television 35.</p>"}],"question":"How do we express preferences correctly and punctuate an opinion text?","tache":"Learn the structures of preference and the main punctuation rules, then rewrite Ali's comment and present the survey results.","hypotheses":["Punctuation is not important on the internet.","Prefer… than and would rather to are correct English.","Prefer… to, would rather + base verb + than, would prefer + to; and punctuation — capitals, full stops, commas, apostrophes — makes the text clear."]},"parties":[{"t":"Prefer, would rather, would prefer","html":"<div class='def'><b>Preference</b>A choice of one thing over another. English expresses it with prefer… to, like… better than, would rather… than and would prefer…, each with its own structure.</div><ul><li><strong>prefer + noun / -ing + to + noun / -ing</strong> (general): <em>I prefer the radio <strong>to</strong> social media. I prefer listening <strong>to</strong> reading.</em></li><li><strong>like… better than</strong>: <em>I like the radio better than television.</em></li><li><strong>would rather + base verb (+ than + base verb)</strong> (a particular situation): <em>I'd rather listen to the news than read it.</em></li><li><strong>would prefer + to-infinitive</strong>: <em>I'd prefer to listen to the news at 7 a.m.</em></li><li><strong>Negative</strong>: <em>I'd rather not use social media for news.</em></li></ul><p class='formule'>prefer A to B ; would rather + verb + than + verb ; would prefer + to + verb</p><div class='ex'><b>General preference and particular choice</b><em>I prefer the radio to social media, but tonight I'd rather watch the match on TV.</em></div><div class='attention'><b>Attention</b>Never <s>prefer… than</s> (say prefer… to) and never <s>would rather to listen</s> (say would rather listen).</div>","planches":[{"type":"2D","titre":"Three structures of preference","legende":"Each structure has its own little word: to, than, to + verb.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Three columns: prefer, would rather and would prefer' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Expressing preferences</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='112.66666666666667' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>prefer</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>prefer A to B</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>prefer -ing to -ing</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ general</text><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='222.33333333333334' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='320' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>would rather</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>+ base verb</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>… than + verb</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>'d rather not</text><text x='232.33333333333334' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ now, this time</text><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='429.6666666666667' y='44' width='195.33333333333334' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='527.3333333333334' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='13.5' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>would prefer</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>+ to + verb</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I'd prefer to listen</text><text x='439.6666666666667' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='11.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ polite</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}],"fil":{"html":"<p>“Prefer… than” and “would rather to listen” are two classic errors: English says “prefer the radio <strong>to</strong> social media” and “would rather <strong>listen</strong>”. Each structure has its own small word.</p>","verdicts":[[1,"rejetee","Prefer… to, would rather + base verb: not prefer… than or would rather to."]]},"retenir":"prefer A to B ; like A better than B ; would rather + verb + than ; would prefer + to + verb ; I'd rather not."},{"t":"Punctuation: capitals, full stops, commas","verrou":true,"illus":{"legende":"The main punctuation marks. Each mark has a job.","svg":"<svg viewBox='0 0 640 210' role='img' aria-label='Four columns: end marks, commas, capital letters and apostrophes' font-family='Inter,Arial,sans-serif'><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#fff'/><defs></defs><rect width='640' height='210' fill='#FBF8F2'/><text x='320' y='28' text-anchor='middle' font-size='15' font-weight='700' fill='#001136'>Punctuation</text><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#1E499B' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='15' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#1E499B'/><text x='86.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>. ? !</text><text x='25' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>full stop: statement</text><text x='25' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>question mark</text><text x='25' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>exclamation mark</text><text x='25' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#1E499B'>→ end</text><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#2E7D32' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='170.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#2E7D32'/><text x='242.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>,</text><text x='180.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>lists</text><text x='180.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>after However,</text><text x='180.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>before but / so</text><text x='180.5' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#2E7D32'>→ pause</text><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#7B3F99' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='326' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#7B3F99'/><text x='397.75' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>Capitals</text><text x='336' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>I, names</text><text x='336' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>towns, days</text><text x='336' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>languages</text><text x='336' y='169' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#7B3F99'>→ start</text><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='152' rx='12' fill='#fff' stroke='#C2540A' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='481.5' y='44' width='143.5' height='34' rx='11' fill='#C2540A'/><text x='553.25' y='66' text-anchor='middle' font-size='12' font-weight='700' fill='#fff'>'</text><text x='491.5' y='100' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>it's = it is</text><text x='491.5' y='123' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='550' fill='#001136'>Ali's blog</text><text x='491.5' y='146' text-anchor='start' font-size='10.5' font-weight='800' fill='#C2540A'>→ apostrophe</text><text x='634' y='205' font-size='8' text-anchor='end' fill='#8A93A6'>Planche VÉRITAS</text></svg>"}},{"t":"The apostrophe: it's or its?","verrou":true},{"t":"Vers le Probatoire","verrou":true}],"revision":[],"exo":"","c":"1re A","rang":59,"m":"anglais","payant":true,"quiz":[],"apc":{"module":"Media and Communication","famille":"Vie sociale et culturelle","agir":"Communicate about media and communication","situation":"In Maroua, Ali answers the school blog question “Radio or social media: which do you prefer for news?” with “i prefer the radio than social media because its more reliable i would rather to listen the news at 7 am”. The survey: 140 of 250 pupils prefer social media, 75 the radio, 35 television.","tache":"Learn the structures of preference and the main punctuation rules, then rewrite Ali's comment and present the survey results."},"verrou":true,"nq":10,"labo":true});
